{
  "Ps.51.17": {
    "text": "We cannot have a broken spirit & be contrite without humility.  See [[Jas.4.6]] God gives grace to the humble.  See the humble publican, [[Luke.18.14]]",
    "created": "2026-06-18T18:57:39.198Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-18T19:11:40.506Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "1John.1.9": {
    "text": "This can be a good scripture to come to after leading someone down the \"Roman Road\" [[Rom.3.23]], [[Rom.6.23]] and [[Rom.10.10]] (Romans 10:9-10) . Only Jesus can cleanse us from all unrighteousness, granting us complete forgiveness.",
    "created": "2026-06-15T23:01:44.960Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-21T21:43:17.593Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Rom.6.23": {
    "text": "The 2nd stop on the \"Roman Road\".  Sin pays you with death, but eternal life is a free gift! Come here from [[Rom.3.23]].  Then, from here, proceed to [[Rom.10.10]] (Romans 10:9-10)",
    "created": "2026-06-15T22:43:38.885Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-21T21:43:27.981Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Rom.4.13": {
    "text": "Faith is the vehicle by which obtain righteousness.  It basically opens the door.  It does not come through works but through a humbling of our hearts turning to the Lord in faith. This is imputed righteousness.",
    "created": "2026-06-20T13:44:48.031Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-20T13:44:53.684Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Heb.11.6": {
    "text": "The is pleased - even delighted - when we put our faith in Him!  See [[Ps.147.11]]",
    "created": "2026-06-16T15:11:28.844Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-16T15:11:28.844Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Gen.2.17": {
    "text": "This is why death reigned, even without a law. [[Rom.5.15]]",
    "created": "2026-06-20T23:53:13.901Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-20T23:53:26.756Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Jas.4.6": {
    "text": "God gives grace to the humble.  When we approach God, we must do so in true humility, recognizing that He is perfect & we are tainted sinners. See the humble publican, [[Luke.18.9]], and David's prayer of repentance, [[Ps.51.17]] (a broken spirit & a contrite heart)",
    "created": "2026-06-18T18:34:36.946Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-18T18:58:48.191Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Luke.3.38": {
    "text": "Adam was called the son of God - but Adam disobeyed and was cast out because of His sin.  Christ is the antitype of Adam: Adam disobeyed, but Christ was obedient, even unto death [[Phil.2.8]]. See [[Rom.5.19]]",
    "created": "2026-06-20T23:57:39.537Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-21T00:00:20.545Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Rom.13.9": {
    "text": "\"briefly comprehended\" = \"summed up\" per [G0346]",
    "created": "2026-06-17T16:14:17.276Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-17T16:14:17.276Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "1Cor.16.14": {
    "text": "As the NLT puts it, \"Do everything in love\". [[Rom.13.10]]  This fulfills the law since love is unselfish and works no evil to its neighbor.",
    "created": "2026-06-17T16:16:08.795Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-17T16:17:52.960Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Rom.10.13": {
    "tags": [
      "Saved"
    ],
    "updated": "2026-07-25T22:18:35.495Z",
    "text": "WHOSOEVER!  See [[Matt.24.13]]  and [[Rom.5.9]] & [[Mark.16.16]]  & [[Acts.16.31]]",
    "created": "2026-07-25T21:29:15.878Z"
  },
  "Rev.5.9": {
    "text": "\"...for thou... hast redeemed us to God by thy blood out of every kindred, and tongue, and people, and nation.\" The 4 beasts & 24 elders are those who have been redeemed - ransomed, saved, justified by faith!  The best song we can sing is one that celebrates our salvation! Go see Revelation 14:2-4 [[Rev.14.4]]",
    "created": "2026-06-16T14:37:51.808Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-16T14:42:15.153Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "1John.1.10": {
    "updated": "2026-07-07T17:37:54.402Z",
    "created": "2026-06-16T01:07:33.388Z",
    "text": "If perfection were possible, this verse would not exist! Same with 1 John 1:8",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Ps.147.11": {
    "text": "The only way to please the Lord is by exercising faith in Him!  See [[Heb.11.6]]",
    "created": "2026-06-16T15:12:17.480Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-16T15:12:17.480Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Rom.10.10": {
    "text": "Romans 10:9-10 is the last stop on the \"Roman Road\" (you should have arrived here after [[Rom.3.23]] and [[Rom.6.23]]).  This tells the person what to do to \"be saved\".   From here you may also go to [[1John.1.9]] to show them that Jesus will forgive all their sins, too. ",
    "created": "2026-06-15T22:52:09.006Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-21T21:43:39.907Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Rev.14.4": {
    "text": "\"These were the redeemed from among men...\" Similar to Revelation 5:9 [[Rev.5.9]], the redeemed are singing a new song (vs 3) to the Lord! One praising Him for their salvation.\nThese passages generally connect a \"new song\" with:\n\n1. God's deliverance [[Ps.40.1]].\n2. God's marvelous works and salvation [[Ps.98.1]]\n3. Worldwide worship of the Lord [[Ps.96.1]], [[Isa.42.1]]\n4. The redemption accomplished by Christ [[Rev.5.1]].\n5. The redeemed worshipping our Savior in heaven [[Rev.14.1]]",
    "created": "2026-06-16T14:44:20.777Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-16T14:59:23.159Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Rom.4.22": {
    "text": "Abraham had righteousness imputed to him because of his strong faith in the Lord. [[Gen.15.6]]",
    "created": "2026-06-20T13:46:05.566Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-20T13:48:15.695Z",
    "tags": []
  },
