    "text": "In Christ - [[Rom.8.1]]",
    "created": "2026-07-22T16:12:11.865Z",
    "tags": [
      "In Christ",
      "New Creature"
    ],
    "updated": "2026-07-22T16:14:18.469Z"
  },
  "Acts.16.31": {
    "tags": [
      "Saved"
    ],
    "updated": "2026-07-25T22:05:06.702Z",
    "text": "To be Saved: [[Matt.24.13]] & [[Rom.5.9]] & [[Rom.10.13]] & [[Mark.16.16]]",
    "created": "2026-07-25T22:03:03.643Z"
  },
  "Gen.15.6": {
    "text": "The word \"counted\" here is châshab (H2803), and both Strongs & Thayer list \"imputed\" as a valid translation.  See [[Rom.5.19]] Especially [[Rom.4.24]] (Romans 4:22-24 - really, the whole chapter!)",
    "created": "2026-06-20T13:30:49.137Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-20T13:47:49.703Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Deut.7.9": {
    "text": "Compare with [[Exod.34.7]], where he imputes the guilt of fathers up to the 3rd/4th generation.  His mercy is 1,000 times more powerful than sin!",
    "created": "2026-06-18T18:13:31.032Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-18T18:15:30.403Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "2Thess.2.10": {
    "text": "they will perish because they don't receive a love of the truth.  We can tie this back to the spiritual indifference Jesus comments on in [[Matt.24.12]] \"the love of many will wax cold.\"",
    "created": "2026-06-18T18:20:15.053Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-18T18:20:26.895Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Rom.5.9": {
    "tags": [
      "Saved"
    ],
    "updated": "2026-07-25T22:18:53.598Z",
    "text": "See also [[Matt.24.13]] and [[Rom.10.13]] & [[Mark.16.16]] & [[Acts.16.31]]",
    "created": "2026-07-25T21:36:07.380Z"
  },
  "Rom.5.19": {
    "text": "Jesus is the antitype of Adam. Adam brought death to all, Jesus brought life to all. Just as Adam's condemnation was imputed to us by Him (he was the earthly father of all), Righteousness was imputed to us by Christ (being the heavenly Father of all who believe).  [[John.3.17]]  See vs 15.  See also [[Luke.3.38]]",
    "created": "2026-06-20T13:37:33.792Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-20T23:58:38.062Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Rom.13.10": {
    "text": "\"Do everything in love.\" [[1Cor.16.14]]",
    "created": "2026-06-17T16:16:46.262Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-17T16:16:46.262Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Luke.18.13": {
    "tags": [],
    "updated": "2026-07-25T14:27:34.723Z",
    "text": "The publican showed true humility, while the Pharisee was concerned more with appearance. See [[Jas.4.6]] see also [[Matt.5.3]] (poor in spirit), and David's prayer of repentance in [[Ps.51.17]]",
    "created": "2026-07-25T14:27:34.723Z"
  },
  "Rom.5.15": {
    "text": "Why did death reign? Because of Adam's condemnation (\"thou shalt surely die\" - [[Gen.2.17]]) was imputed to all his offspring, even though there was no law, nor was there any direct disobedience to God's commandment. (see vs 19)",
    "created": "2026-06-20T23:19:03.740Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-20T23:52:26.115Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Gen.1.2": {
    "text": "Spirit of God \"moved\" upon the face of the waters.  Moved = râchaph\n\"fluttered\".",
    "created": "2026-06-16T19:06:21.482Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-16T19:06:21.482Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Deut.5.9": {
    "text": "Although the iniquity of the fathers will be visited upon the 3rd and 4th generation, look at [[Deut.7.9]]",
    "created": "2026-07-06T23:19:00.000Z",
    "updated": "2026-07-06T23:19:00.000Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Luke.7.47": {
    "text": "A person who has forgiven much, loves much. One that is forgiven little, loves little.  To be forgiven much causes great humility, realizing how unworthy we are of such grace & mercy!",
    "created": "2026-06-18T19:43:37.578Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-18T19:43:37.578Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Rom.10.15": {
    "updated": "2026-07-21T12:10:44.656Z",
    "created": "2026-07-21T12:05:54.087Z",
    "text": "Quoted from [[Isa.52.7]]. See also Paul's teaching on the armor of God [[Eph.6.15]]",
    "tags": [
      "Peace",
      "gospel"
    ]
  },
  "Rom.3.23": {
    "text": "The beginning of the \"Roman Road\" for sharing the gospel. We're all sinners.\nNext in line should be [[Rom.6.23]], then finally [[Rom.10.10]] (Romans 10:9-10)",
    "created": "2026-06-16T00:38:20.871Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-21T21:43:54.125Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Luke.18.14": {
    "text": "See [[Jas.4.6]] God gives grace to the humble.  See [[Ps.51.17]], David's repentance.  \"a broken and contrite heart\"",
    "created": "2026-06-18T18:37:31.230Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-18T19:17:10.056Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "John.3.18": {
    "text": "Christ doesn't condemn you because you don't believe in Him - we were already condemned before He came.  We were condemned from birth because of Adam's sin. He imputed condemnation to us.  Conversely, Christ imputes His righteousness to those who put their faith in Him.  See [[Rom.5.19]] (Romans 5:12-19 for full discourse from Paul). See the account of Abram's faith/obedience [[Gen.15.6]]",
    "created": "2026-06-20T13:25:33.330Z",
    "tags": [
      "Condemnation"
    ],
    "updated": "2026-07-22T16:10:57.342Z"
  },
  "Matt.24.12": {
    "text": "Tie this to [[2Thess.2.1]], where it says that they will perish because they don't receive a love of the truth!    Love is translated from the Greek \"agape\"\n\nIn Missler's teaching, \"love\" here includes:\n* Love for the Lord.\n* Love for God's Word.\n* Love for fellow believers.\n* Compassion for others.",
    "created": "2026-06-18T18:18:10.817Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-18T18:23:22.189Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Mark.15.21": {
    "text": "Rufus, Simon's son, is mentioned by Paul in [[Rom.16.13]]",
    "created": "2026-06-20T13:55:39.523Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-20T13:55:46.763Z",
    "tags": []
  },
  "Rom.12.1": {
    "text": "...your reasonable \"service\":  Service = Worship per [G2999]. ",
    "created": "2026-06-17T16:11:17.109Z",
    "updated": "2026-06-17T16:11:17.109Z",
    "tags": []
  }
